    "text": {
     "en": "The Big Laddoo is a funny poem to recite. It asks us to imagine all laddoos becoming one big laddoo.\nThen it imagines all children becoming one big child and all seas becoming one big sea.\nFinally the big child picks the big laddoo and throws it into the big sea. What a big splish-splash!\nThe poem plays with the word BIG and with sounds like splish-splash.\nIn the book you tell about the biggest thing you have eaten, and list round things that can be eaten and cannot be eaten.\nNew words: sea, splish-splash."
    }
